  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Uncle Junior** (1 review): Cited as a prime example of the show's jazzy, experimental, extended approach [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Solid**: back after 83 archived shows (848 days) [4]\n- **Neal solo**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Solid**: back after 83 archived shows (848 days) [4]\n- **Nautilus**: back after 36 archived shows (579 days); rare: 4 archived performances [4]\n- **Alan solo**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2003-02-19.flac** (recommended): source not stated; 15 songs; 156 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests included Joshua Redman on tenor sax, Kenny Garrett on alto sax, and Stefon Harris on electric vibes [1]\n- Jay Rodriquez also guested, playing baritone and tenor saxes and flute [1]\n- Soulive usually stuck to a set format; this show was a rare occasion where they stretched out and jammed more [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2003-02-19.flac**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by ?; source: Neumann TLM 170s (omnis @ PAs) > Apogee AD 1000 > Teac DAP20 [1]",
